ChurchCRM itself is not vendored into this repository. This repo contains only
deployment configuration, and builds the application from the **official
release artifact** published by the ChurchCRM project
(`ChurchCRM-<version>.zip`, GitHub Releases). `build.sh` verifies that artifact
against the SHA-256 digest recorded in the GitHub Releases API before building,
so no application source is forked or re-hosted here.

## What was reused from upstream, verbatim

These files are taken from the ChurchCRM repository (MIT, same terms) and are
used unmodified:

| File | Upstream path |
|---|---|
| Apache + PHP 8.4 image, all stages | `docker/Dockerfile.churchcrm-apache-php8` |
| Release-archive extractor | `docker/prepare-release-context.py` |
| Apache server config | `docker/apache/default.conf` |

`build.sh` clones upstream and invokes these directly, so credit stays with the
original authors and upstream fixes are picked up automatically.

