## Upstream authors and contributors

ChurchCRM is built by its contributors. The full list, as recorded by GitHub, is
at <https://github.com/churchcrm/crm/graphs/contributors>. Rather than copy a
list that goes stale, this repository links to the canonical page.

The Docker packaging in the upstream repository — including the production
Dockerfiles, the release-image publish workflow, the checksum verification and
the security notes in `docker/DOCKER_RELEASE.md` — was written and reviewed by
the ChurchCRM maintainers. This repository depends on that work and deliberately
does not duplicate or replace it. In particular, the release-image pipeline that
upstream designed has never been executed (see below).

## Why this repository exists

The upstream `docker-release.yml` workflow, which would publish versioned images
to Docker Hub, triggers on `release: published` and has **zero runs**, so the
tags documented in upstream's `docker/DOCKER_RELEASE.md`
(`latest-php8-apache`, `<version>-php8-apache`) do not exist on Docker Hub. The
only images in the `churchcrm/crm` Docker Hub repository are from 2018 and
predate PHP 8.

Upstream's `docker/examples/` compose files are documented by upstream as *not*
working recipes ("they are not working release-image recipes"). This repository
supplies a stack that has been verified end to end.

Fixing the missing upstream publish is the better long-term answer and is the
ChurchCRM maintainers' to make. Until then, images are built from the official,
checksum-verified release artifacts.

